      "content": "While leaf damage like round holes with scalloped edges and small white spots could indicate spider mite or thrips infestations, it can also be misdiagnosed as deficiencies such as phosphorus (which might appear as tiny black or brown spots) or eventually rot in acidic soil. Since your soil test only indicated low nitrogen so far, these pests are the more likely culprit given the rapid 'overnight' timing. Inspecting healthy, new growth for tiny webbing or squished insects will help confirm an infestation over a nutrient issue.",
